The smart group panel of the SearchKit admin UI shows no group type options.

Its template asks getField() for the Group fields description, group_type and
visibility by passing the entity 'Group'. crmSearchAdminGroup's getField()
drops that argument and looks the fields up on the saved search instead.

Upstream: https://github.com/civicrm/civicrm-core/pull/37549
Since: 6.19.1

diff --git a/ext/search_kit/ang/crmSearchAdmin/crmSearchAdminGroup.component.js b/ext/search_kit/ang/crmSearchAdmin/crmSearchAdminGroup.component.js
index 40851e80c0..7084036a7a 100644
--- a/ext/search_kit/ang/crmSearchAdmin/crmSearchAdminGroup.component.js
+++ b/ext/search_kit/ang/crmSearchAdmin/crmSearchAdminGroup.component.js
@@ -10,7 +10,7 @@
       const ts = $scope.ts = CRM.ts('org.civicrm.search_kit');
 
       this.getEntity = searchMeta.getEntity;
-      this.getField = (fieldName) => searchMeta.getField(fieldName, this.savedSearch);
+      this.getField = (fieldName, entity) => searchMeta.getField(fieldName, entity || this.savedSearch);
 
       this.smartGroupColumns = [];
 
